NNAAMMEE
       rrlogind  -  Road Runner Login Daemon. A suitable replace-
       ment for it's Perl counterpart.

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
       rrrrllooggiinndd [[--pp <<ppoorrtt>>]] [[--vv]] [[--kk]] [[--dd]] [[--tt]]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
       rrrrllooggiinndd is for use in those  areas  that  are  using  the
       "Road  Runner  Client Server Session Management Protocol".
       These areas include, but are not limited to: North Eastern
       Ohio,  Columbus Ohio, Austin Texas, Hawaii, Tampa Bay Fla,
       and Charlotte NC.

       This daemon  is  designed  to  replace  the  _r_r_l_o_g_i_n  Perl
       script. It implements the entire _S_e_s_s_i_o_n _M_a_n_a_g_e_r _P_r_o_t_o_c_o_l_,
       instead of just the login portion.

OOPPTTIIOONNSS
       _-_p _<_p_o_r_t_>      Used to change  the  default  (60000)  port
                      number   to   communicate   with   for  the
                      login server.

       _-_v             Turns on verbose mode.

       _-_d             Turns on debugging mode.

       _-_k             Kills any running instance of  rrrrllooggiinndd  or
                      removes the stale pid file.

       _-_t             Always trust the server to be authentic.

CCHHAANNGGEESS
       _v_1_._0 - Initial Release 11/30/1998
              A very buggy alpha version of the client

       _v_1_._1 - Major Bug Fix and 1st Official Release 12/03/1998
              Fixed keep-alive support.
              Finished implementing the protocol specs.

       _v_1_._2 - Bug Fixes 12/14/1998, Feature Additions
              Fixed a small bug in the client state loop.
              Changed  all  the  syslog  messages  to  report  as
                 LOG_INFO (Now only logs to messages  instead  of
                 all error conditions being sent to syslog.)
              Altered  listener  code  to  also  work under 2.1.x
                 kernels.
              Added "Always Trust" parameter  to  compensate  for
                 some non-spec-compliant auth servers.
              Added broken-session detection code.

       _v_1_._3 - Bug Fixes 01/17/1999, Feature Additions
               Fixed  segmentation  fault  when  username was not
                 specified.



